{
  "company_name": "PetroLedger Corp",
  "industry": "Oil & Gas Integrated",
  "use_case": "Financial analytics and reporting for integrated oil and gas operations",
  "space_title": "PetroLedger Corp - Financial Analytics & Reporting 💰",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Oil & Gas Integrated\n\n**Use case:** Financial Analytics & Reporting\n\nPetroLedger Corp — corporate financial analytics across 20 cost centers spanning Upstream, Downstream, Midstream, and Corporate divisions globally. FP&A and Controllership use this space to track revenue vs. plan, OPEX/CAPEX variance, and division-level EBITDA day-to-day; the CFO and divisional VPs use it to monitor operating margin, ROIC, OPEX per BOE, and budget adherence ahead of board and investor reporting cycles.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Revenue ($MM) — top-line, actual vs. planned\n- EBITDA ($MM) — earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation, amortization\n- Operating margin (%) — IOC top-quartile >20% in mid-cycle environments\n- ROIC (%) — capital efficiency; IOC target 8-12%\n- OPEX per BOE ($/BOE) — lifting cost benchmark; majors target <12 $/BOE upstream\n- Budget variance (%) — actual vs. plan at cost center / GL category\n- Total CAPEX ($MM) — capital deployed by division\n- G&A spend ($MM) — overhead trend\n\n**Data sources**\n- `financial_transactions` — daily revenue, OPEX, CAPEX, D&A, G&A by cost center and GL category\n- `budget_snapshots` — monthly planned vs. actual revenue and OPEX, plus EBITDA\n- `financial_kpi_monthly` — operating margin, ROIC, OPEX/BOE, headcount by cost center",
  "schema_basename": "og_integrated_finance",
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "financial_transactions",
      "description": "Daily financial transactions including revenue, operating expenses, and capital expenditures by cost center.",
      "columns": [
