  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Financial Analytics and Reporting for an integrated oil & gas major running 20 cost centers across Upstream (GoM / Permian / Alaska / North Sea / West Africa / LNG), Downstream (refining / petchem / retail / lubricants / renewable fuels), Midstream (pipelines / NGL / marine / storage), and Corporate functions. Stakeholders include FP&A and Controllership (revenue vs. plan, variance, EBITDA), the CFO (margin, ROIC, lifting cost), and divisional VPs (cost-center performance vs. budget).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Revenue / OPEX / CAPEX = amount_usd on financial_transactions, filtered by account_type\n- Operating margin = operating_margin_pct on financial_kpi_monthly; IOC top-quartile >20% mid-cycle\n- ROIC = roic_pct on financial_kpi_monthly; IOC target 8-12% through the cycle\n- OPEX/BOE = opex_per_boe on financial_kpi_monthly; majors target <12 USD/BOE upstream lifting cost\n- EBITDA = ebitda_usd on budget_snapshots\n- Budget variance = (actual - planned) / planned on budget_snapshots (revenue or opex)\n- GL categories = Production / Exploration / Refining / Marketing / Transportation / Admin\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - financial_transactions_metrics (source: financial_transactions) — dims: transaction_date, cost_center_id, division, region, account_type, gl_category; measures: total_amount_usd, total_budget_usd, total_transactions, avg_transaction_usd, max_amount.\n  - budget_snapshots_metrics (source: budget_snapshots) — dims: snapshot_month, cost_center_id, division, region; measures: total_actual_revenue, total_planned_revenue, total_actual_opex, total_ebitda, total_planned_opex, max_planned_revenue.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. cost_center_name, operating_margin_pct, roic_pct, opex_per_boe, headcount).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
